:question/problem "Find the entry $a_{23}$ of the matrix ${A},$ where \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry $a_{23}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $3$rd column. Therefore, $a_{23}={\\color{blue}{-3}}.$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4372"] :question/problem "Find the entry $b_{22}$ of the matrix ${B},$ where \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry $b_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, $b_{22}={\\color{blue}{2}}.$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4373"] :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $C$ given below. Describe it in terms of $c_{ij}.$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 34 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry lies at the intersection of the $1$st row and $3$rd column. Therefore, we have $c_{13}={\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{5}}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
